                <pb facs="0230" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg164"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/908: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-15T12:00:00-05:00">August 15,
                        1934—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 1:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>394. My telegram 380, August 10, noon. Cuban officials state they desire
                    reduction of consular fees “on and after July 1, 1935.”since estimated receipts
                    (difference of over one million pesos) included in this year’s budget.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
